<body id="artifacts-component-root-html">
    <!-- Download Section -->
    <div class="download-section" style="display: none;">
        <h2 style="color: white; border: none; margin: 0;">📄 Download Report as Word Document</h2>
        <p style="margin: 15px 0;">Click the button below to download this report in .docx format</p>
        <button class="download-btn" onclick="downloadAsWord()">⬇️ Download Report (.docx)</button>
        <button class="download-btn" onclick="window.print()">🖨️ Print Report</button>
    </div>

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="header">
        <h1>Course Registration &amp; Enrollment System</h1>
        <p><strong>Web Engineering (CSC-324) – Assignment 3</strong></p>
        <p>Instructor: Syed Nouman Ali Shah</p>
        <p>Submission Date: November 15, 2025</p>
    </div>

    <div class="info-box">
        <p><strong>Student Name:</strong> [Your Name Here]</p>
        <p><strong>Roll Number:</strong> [Your Roll No Here]</p>
        <p><strong>Program:</strong> BS Computer Science</p>
        <p><strong>Semester:</strong> 5th</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Executive Summary -->
    <h2>Executive Summary</h2>
    <p>
        This report documents the development of a comprehensive Course Registration and Enrollment System 
        built using Spring Boot for the backend and React for the frontend. The system implements a complete 
        domain model for managing students, courses, and registrations with robust business rule validation 
        and RESTful API architecture.
    </p>
    
    <p><strong>Technology Stack:</strong></p>
    <div style="margin: 15px 0;">
        <span class="tech-stack">Spring Boot 3.x</span>
        <span class="tech-stack">Spring Data JPA</span>
        <span class="tech-stack">MySQL Database</span>
        <span class="tech-stack">React 18</span>
        <span class="tech-stack">React Router</span>
        <span class="tech-stack">Axios</span>
        <span class="tech-stack">RESTful APIs</span>
    </div>

    <div class="page-break"></div>

    <!-- Part 1: Domain Model -->
    <h2>Part 1: Domain Model &amp; JPA Entities</h2>
    
    <h3>1.1 Entity Design &amp; Relationships</h3>
    <p>
        The system implements three core entities with proper JPA mappings and bidirectional relationships:
    </p>

    <h4>Student Entity</h4>
    <table>
        <tbody><tr>
            <th>Attribute</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Constraints</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>id</td>
            <td>Long</td>
            <td>Primary Key, Auto-generated</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>rollNo</td>
            <td>String</td>
            <td>Unique, Not Null</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>name</td>
            <td>String</td>
            <td>Not Null</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>email</td>
            <td>String</td>
            <td>Unique, Valid Email Format</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>program</td>
            <td>String</td>
            <td>Not Null (e.g., BSCS, BSE)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>semester</td>
            <td>Integer</td>
            <td>Min: 1, Max: 8</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody></table>

    <h4>Course Entity</h4>
    <table>
        <tbody><tr>
            <th>Attribute</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Constraints</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>id</td>
            <td>Long</td>
            <td>Primary Key, Auto-generated</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>code</td>
            <td>String</td>
            <td>Unique, Not Null (e.g., CSC-324)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>title</td>
            <td>String</td>
            <td>Not Null</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>creditHours</td>
            <td>Integer</td>
            <td>Min: 1, Max: 6</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>maxSeats</td>
            <td>Integer</td>
            <td>Min: 1</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>prerequisite</td>
            <td>Course</td>
            <td>Self-reference (Optional)</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody></table>

    <h4>Registration Entity</h4>
    <table>
        <tbody><tr>
            <th>Attribute</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Constraints</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>id</td>
            <td>Long</td>
            <td>Primary Key, Auto-generated</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>student</td>
            <td>Student</td>
            <td>Many-to-One, Not Null</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>course</td>
            <td>Course</td>
            <td>Many-to-One, Not Null</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>semester</td>
            <td>String</td>
            <td>Not Null (e.g., Fall 2025)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>status</td>
            <td>Enum</td>
            <td>REGISTERED, COMPLETED, DROPPED</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>grade</td>
            <td>String</td>
            <td>Optional (A, A-, B+, etc.)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>registrationDate</td>
            <td>LocalDate</td>
            <td>Auto-set on creation</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody></table>

    <h3>1.2 JPA Annotations &amp; Validations</h3>
    <p>Key JPA annotations implemented:</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>@Entity</strong> - Marks classes as JPA entities</li>
        <li><strong>@Id &amp; @GeneratedValue</strong> - Primary key with auto-increment strategy</li>
        <li><strong>@ManyToOne &amp; @OneToMany</strong> - Bidirectional relationships</li>
        <li><strong>@JoinColumn</strong> - Foreign key column definitions</li>
        <li><strong>@NotNull, @NotBlank</strong> - Bean validation</li>
        <li><strong>@Email</strong> - Email format validation</li>
        <li><strong>@Min, @Max</strong> - Numeric range validation</li>
        <li><strong>@Enumerated</strong> - Enum type mapping for status</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>1.3 Repository Layer</h3>
    <p>Custom query methods implemented in repositories:</p>
    
    <div class="code-block">
// StudentRepository
Optional&lt;Student&gt; findByRollNo(String rollNo);
Optional&lt;Student&gt; findByEmail(String email);

// CourseRepository  
Optional&lt;Course&gt; findByCode(String code);

// RegistrationRepository
List&lt;Registration&gt; findByStudentId(Long studentId);
List&lt;Registration&gt; findByCourseId(Long courseId);
List&lt;Registration&gt; findBySemester(String semester);
List&lt;Registration&gt; findByStudentIdAndStatus(Long studentId, RegistrationStatus status);
    </div>

    <h3>1.4 Sample Data Seeding</h3>
    <p>
        A <strong>DataLoader</strong> component seeds the database with initial data on application startup:
    </p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
        <li>5 Students with diverse programs (BSCS, BSE, BSDS)</li>
        <li>5 Courses with prerequisite relationships (CSC-201 → CSC-324)</li>
        <li>5 Sample registrations with different statuses</li>
    </ul>

