    <h2>Key Features &amp; Achievements</h2>

    <h3>6.1 Core Features Implemented</h3>
    <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>Complete CRUD Operations</strong> - All entities support Create, Read, Update, Delete</li>
        <li><strong>Business Rule Validation</strong> - Three comprehensive rules enforced at service layer</li>
        <li><strong>RESTful API Design</strong> - Proper HTTP methods, status codes, and JSON responses</li>
        <li><strong>Exception Handling</strong> - Centralized error handling with consistent JSON format</li>
        <li><strong>Data Validation</strong> - Bean validation with @NotNull, @Email, @Min, @Max annotations</li>
        <li><strong>Bidirectional Relationships</strong> - Proper JPA mappings with cascade and fetch strategies</li>
        <li><strong>Prerequisite System</strong> - Self-referencing course prerequisite with validation</li>
        <li><strong>Real-time Search</strong> - Client-side filtering with instant results</li>
        <li><strong>Modal-based Registration</strong> - Clean UX with overlay and form validation</li>
        <li><strong>Status Management</strong> - Enum-based status tracking (REGISTERED, COMPLETED, DROPPED)</li>
        <li><strong>Student Dashboard</strong> - Comprehensive view with statistics and filtering</li>
        <li><strong>Responsive Design</strong> - Mobile-friendly interface with adaptive layouts</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>6.2 Additional Enhancements</h3>
    <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>Custom Query Methods</strong> - Derived queries in repositories for complex filtering</li>
        <li><strong>Data Seeding</strong> - Automatic population of sample data on startup</li>
        <li><strong>Grade Tracking</strong> - Optional grade field for completed courses</li>
        <li><strong>Registration Date</strong> - Automatic timestamp on registration creation</li>
        <li><strong>Category Filtering</strong> - Frontend categorization by course type</li>
        <li><strong>Loading States</strong> - User feedback during asynchronous operations</li>
        <li><strong>Empty States</strong> - Helpful messages when no data is available</li>
        <li><strong>Alert System</strong> - Color-coded success/error notifications with auto-dismiss</li>
        <li><strong>Prerequisite Warnings</strong> - Visual indicators for courses requiring prerequisites</li>
        <li><strong>Statistics Cards</strong> - Real-time counts of registration statuses</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>6.3 Code Quality Practices</h3>
    <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>Clean Architecture</strong> - Clear separation between layers (Controller → Service → Repository)</li>
        <li><strong>Single Responsibility</strong> - Each class/component has one focused purpose</li>
        <li><strong>DRY Principle</strong> - Reusable components and utility functions</li>
        <li><strong>Consistent Naming</strong> - Standard conventions across backend and frontend</li>
        <li><strong>Error Handling</strong> - Try-catch blocks with meaningful error messages</li>
        <li><strong>Type Safety</strong> - Proper use of TypeScript-ready patterns</li>
        <li><strong>Code Comments</strong> - Documentation for complex business logic</li>
        <li><strong>Git Best Practices</strong> - Meaningful commit messages and branching</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="page-break"></div>

    <!-- Challenges & Solutions -->
    <h2>Challenges &amp; Solutions</h2>

    <h3>7.1 Technical Challenges</h3>

    <div class="warning-box">
        <h4>Challenge 1: Circular Dependency in Prerequisite Validation</h4>
        <p><strong>Problem:</strong> Validating prerequisites required checking if a student has completed a course, which could lead to infinite loops in self-referencing relationships.</p>
        <p><strong>Solution:</strong> Implemented explicit null checks and status-based queries to break the circular reference chain. Used EXISTS query instead of fetching full entities.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="warning-box">
        <h4>Challenge 2: CORS Policy Blocking API Requests</h4>
        <p><strong>Problem:</strong> React frontend on localhost:3000 was blocked from accessing Spring Boot backend on localhost:8080 due to CORS policy.</p>
        <p><strong>Solution:</strong> Added @CrossOrigin annotation to all controllers with explicit origin whitelisting. Configured proper CORS headers for preflight requests.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="warning-box">
        <h4>Challenge 3: Managing Bidirectional Relationships</h4>
        <p><strong>Problem:</strong> JSON serialization caused infinite recursion with bidirectional @OneToMany relationships.</p>
        <p><strong>Solution:</strong> Used DTOs instead of directly serializing entities. Carefully applied @JsonManagedReference and @JsonBackReference where needed.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="warning-box">
        <h4>Challenge 4: Real-time Data Synchronization</h4>
        <p><strong>Problem:</strong> After successful registration, course list didn't reflect updated seat availability.</p>
        <p><strong>Solution:</strong> Implemented data refresh mechanism that re-fetches course list after successful registration, ensuring UI stays in sync with backend state.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>7.2 Design Decisions</h3>

    <table>
        <tbody><tr>
            <th>Decision</th>
            <th>Rationale</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Enum for Registration Status</td>
            <td>Type-safe, prevents invalid status values, easier to maintain</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>DTO Pattern for Registration</td>
            <td>Decouples API from entity structure, allows flexible request/response formats</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Service Layer for Business Logic</td>
            <td>Keeps controllers thin, makes business rules reusable and testable</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Custom Exception Classes</td>
            <td>Provides semantic error handling, enables specific error messages</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Modal for Registration Form</td>
            <td>Reduces page navigation, provides focused user experience</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Component-based Frontend</td>
            <td>Promotes reusability, easier maintenance, clear separation of concerns</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody></table>

    <div class="page-break"></div>

